From f60751de32f698e9c60a56206c25a30b1e07f972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:50:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: what a converted render that failed composed
 is said after its errors

render() (dvbridge_render_rgb(), dvbridge_render_packed(), the transport converted to BT.2020) set
base_refused and composed from r->ready before the errors that libplacebo reports for the render
(pl_renderer_get_errors()) turned a render that pl_render_image() had made into a failed one: an
enhancement layer that cannot be sampled ("an EL sampling failure can otherwise return a
successfully rendered BL-only frame"), a hook that was disabled. A render failed that way said
DVBRIDGE_COMPOSED_CCM or DVBRIDGE_COMPOSED_RESHAPING; and over a base layer that is not in PQ, drawn
by libplacebo's reshaping (one in HLG whose RPU declares its picture in PQ, with the composer of ETSI
GS CCM 001 off), DVBRIDGE_BASE_PQ, so the player information gave no "hlgbase" or "sdrbase" reason
for it. Both are set now after the errors, as render_hdr10() sets them: a render that its errors
fail composed nothing. Only these two values change; what is drawn, and whether the frame is ready,
do not.

Checked on the host, with the bridge and libplacebo built for it on Mesa's software OpenGL ES (zink
over lavapipe), AddressSanitizer and UBSan: the first base-layer picture of a profile 7 stream, over
PQ, SDR and HLG, with the composer of the clause and with the reshaping, as it comes and with an
error that libplacebo reports after the drawing (its pl_renderer_get_errors() wrapped at link
time): 15 of 15 checks; on the tree before, 5 fail (four renders failed by their errors said what
they had composed, and the one over HLG drawn by the reshaping gave no reason).
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
index 069460b..789f30b 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
@@ -1216,18 +1216,20 @@ static bool render(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct pl_frame *source,
     }
     time_render(r, &params);
     r->ready = pl_render_image(r->renderer, &image, &target, &params) && mask.called && !mask.failed;
-    /* (Hades: a picture over HLG whose RPU declares PQ may be drawn by libplacebo's reshaping) */
-    r->base_refused = r->base_transfer && !ccm_composed && !r->ready ? r->base_transfer
-                                                                    : DVBRIDGE_BASE_PQ;
-    r->composed = !r->ready      ? DVBRIDGE_COMPOSED_NONE
-                  : ccm_composed ? DVBRIDGE_COMPOSED_CCM
-                                 : DVBRIDGE_COMPOSED_RESHAPING;
     /* An EL sampling failure can otherwise return a successfully rendered BL-only frame. A composer of
      * ETSI GS CCM 001 that failed on this GPU is not one: libplacebo composed the picture by its own
      * reshaping, as with it turned off, and said so in the log. */
     struct pl_render_errors errors = pl_renderer_get_errors(r->renderer);
     r->ready = r->ready && !(errors.errors & ~PL_RENDER_ERR_DOVI_COMPOSER) &&
                !errors.num_disabled_hooks;
+    /* (Hades: a picture over HLG whose RPU declares PQ may be drawn by libplacebo's reshaping.) What
+     * the render composed, and why a base layer that is not in PQ was not composed, are of the render
+     * as its errors leave it, as render_hdr10() has them: a render that they fail composed nothing. */
+    r->base_refused = r->base_transfer && !ccm_composed && !r->ready ? r->base_transfer
+                                                                    : DVBRIDGE_BASE_PQ;
+    r->composed = !r->ready      ? DVBRIDGE_COMPOSED_NONE
+                  : ccm_composed ? DVBRIDGE_COMPOSED_CCM
+                                 : DVBRIDGE_COMPOSED_RESHAPING;
     r->early_mask = mask.early_mask;
     if (!packed && (whole || !r->ready))
         r->rgb_clean = false;
